A state $x$ has minimal period $n$ under $f$ when $f^n(x)=x$ and no smaller positive iterate returns to $x$. An observation $h$ is dynamically consistent when $h(f(x))=g(h(x))$. Iterating gives $h(f^n(x))=g^n(h(x))$. Therefore $n$ is a return time of $h(x)$. The minimal observed return $d$ divides every return time, hence $d\mid n$.

For background, see the [Encyclopedia of Mathematics entry on dynamical systems](https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Dynamical_system) and [divisibility](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Divisibility_rule).
